            <ArticleTitle>[A case of glossopharyngeal neuralgia with paroxysmal asystole].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>448-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 74-year-old patients is described who had typical attacks of glossopharyngeal neuralgia associated with very frequent episodes of cardiac arrest. Pacemaker implantation made possible controlling of episodes of cardiac arrest while full remission of attacks was obtained after carbamazepine treatment 900 mg daily.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
